From: FlaxAdvisors
Subject: Return CommandNotAvailable for Get POH Counter

phosphor-chassis-state-manager (which provides the
xyz.openbmc_project.State.PowerOnHours D-Bus interface) is not
installed on this platform. Without it, the handler throws and
returns responseUnspecifiedError. Return D5 (CommandNotAvailable)
instead so callers get a clear "not supported" response.

--- a/chassishandler.cpp
+++ b/chassishandler.cpp
@@ -2831,17 +2831,7 @@
               >
     ipmiGetPOHCounter()
 {
-    // sd_bus error
-    try
-    {
-        return ipmi::responseSuccess(static_cast<uint8_t>(poh::minutesPerCount),
-                                     getPOHCounter());
-    }
-    catch (const std::exception& e)
-    {
-        lg2::error("getPOHCounter error: {ERROR}", "ERROR", e);
-        return ipmi::responseUnspecifiedError();
-    }
+    return ipmi::responseCommandNotAvailable();
 }

 ipmi::RspType<uint3_t, // policy support
